Unless maybe this is going to end up being a situation where (again
MASSIVE SPOILERS for who has not seen the movie Oldboy
) it's an Oldboyesque scenario where Maya ends up being Akira's daughter, hence why her memories were deleted as she would have to remember her Mom or whoever raised her and where she came from. Ayane even shortly mentions how alike Maya and Akira are. Now this might of course lose a bit of its impact, given he is basically already doing that with Ami, but the difference, I guess, being that Ami is doing it willingly and knowingly, while Maya might have been coerced into doing it by certain entities (erasing her memory) for some ultimate goal, completely left in the dark that her lover is also her Dad. Maybe Ami actually is only so much into screwing her Dad, simply because she knows about the consequence of Maya baring a child with Akira and is somehow trying to emulate her and "taking her place". I don't know, this theory is kind of getting out of hand. I guess I just really like the movie Oldboy. But yeah, maybe there is an ounce of something sensible in there.

